course: dictionary
lesson: 15072
title: Rigged: unfair, rigged up, and ropes
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Rigged is a word with more than one meaning, so the context tells you which one it is. «The game was rigged, so the same team won every time.» Here rigged means secretly arranged to be unfair, so one side always wins.
explain: Rigged can also mean fitted with ropes and sails. «The ship was rigged with three tall masts.» Nobody is cheating here. A ship that is rigged has its sails and ropes set up, ready to sail.
explain: Rig up is a phrase on its own. «We rigged up a shelter with an old sheet.» It means made quickly from whatever you have. Ask yourself: is someone cheating, or is something being built? The clues will tell you.
fact: Rigged means unfairly arranged so that a certain person wins, like «a rigged game».
fact: Rigged can also mean fitted with ropes, sails or equipment, like «a ship rigged with three masts».
fact: Rigged up means made quickly from whatever you have, like «rigged up a shelter».
fact: When people say an election was rigged, it is a serious claim, and it needs proof.
fact: Common phrases: «rigged game», «rigged election», «rig up», «the game is rigged».
exercise: «The game was rigged, so the same team won every time.» What does rigged mean here? | Painted bright red | Made quickly from spare things | *Unfairly arranged so one side wins | Fitted with ropes and sails
exercise: «The ship was rigged with three tall masts.» What does rigged mean here? | Unfairly arranged to cheat | *Fitted with sails and ropes | Broken and sinking | Made from old cardboard boxes
exercise: «We rigged up a shelter with an old sheet.» What does rigged up mean? | Cleaned very carefully | *Made quickly from whatever we had | Bought from a shop | Took down and put away
test: «Some people said the election was rigged, but they had no proof.» What does a rigged election mean? | An election with lots of sails | *An election where the result was unfairly fixed | A very fast election | An election held outdoors
test: Kofi wants to rig up a circuit for his science model. What does rig up mean here? | Paint | *Put together quickly from what is available | Sell to a friend | Break apart
exam: Which phrase means a ship fitted with sails? | a rigged vote | *a ship rigged with three masts | rigged up a shelter | a rigged raffle
